# Doc Maintenance

When editing any of the following, update the corresponding reference doc:

| Source file | Reference doc to update |
|---|---|
| `src/config.ts` | `docs/reference/config-schema.md` |
| `package.json` (configuration properties) | `docs/reference/config-schema.md` |
| `src/mcpServer.ts` (tool registrations) | `docs/reference/mcp-tools.md` |
| `package.json` (commands, keybindings) | `docs/reference/commands-and-shortcuts.md` |
| New `src/*.ts` module | `docs/guides/handoff.md` (module table) |

## Update rules

- **Config change**: add/remove/rename config key → update the corresponding table row in `config-schema.md`
- **New MCP tool**: add tool to `mcp-tools.md` following existing format (name, description, parameters table, return value, example)
- **New command**: add to `commands-and-shortcuts.md` commands table
- **New src/ module**: add a row to the module table in `docs/guides/handoff.md`

## When NOT to update

- Changing internal implementation without touching the public interface
- Refactoring private functions not mentioned in docs
- Adding tests (tests don't need doc updates)

## Skill reference

For writing style and formatting conventions, read `.cursor/skills/doc-writer/SKILL.md`.
For reviewing doc accuracy, run `/doc-review` or read `.cursor/skills/doc-reviewer/SKILL.md`.
